# Connect IQ build config - BETA variant.
#
# Identical to monkey.jungle except for the manifest: this one points at
# manifest.beta.xml, which carries a separate application id so the beta
# installs alongside the production app.
#
# Source (source/) and resources (resources/) are still picked up
# automatically. The SDK's default jungle sets `base.sourcePath = .\**.mc` and
# `base.resourcePath = resources` before this file is read, and those defaults
# are keyed off the project directory, NOT off the jungle file's name - a
# non-default jungle name does not change them. Verified by building this
# jungle: it compiles source/*.mc, and manifest.beta.xml's
# name="@Strings.AppNameBeta" resolves, which it could not do if resources/
# were missing from the build.
project.manifest = manifest.beta.xml
